1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,090
听：A Volcano Eruption.

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,181
跟读：A Volcano Eruption.

3
00:00:04,181 --> 00:00:28,915
听：As the best candidate, I was appointed to collect and evaluate information for a database about diverse natural disasters, such as hurricanes, typhoons or thunderstorms. Sometimes I did this by giving out questionnaires to those who went through them. But sometimes I had to go through actual disasters myself.

4
00:00:28,915 --> 00:00:53,650
跟读：As the best candidate, I was appointed to collect and evaluate information for a database about diverse natural disasters, such as hurricanes, typhoons or thunderstorms. Sometimes I did this by giving out questionnaires to those who went through them. But sometimes I had to go through actual disasters myself.

5
00:00:53,650 --> 00:01:16,215
听：The Musaki Volcano was one of them. At that time, I lived in a bungalow alongside the volcano with a novelist, who came for the appreciation of its eruption. One day, when I was drawing diagrams on the balcony and he was bathing inside, the volcano erupted unexpectedly.

6
00:01:16,215 --> 00:01:38,780
跟读：The Musaki Volcano was one of them. At that time, I lived in a bungalow alongside the volcano with a novelist, who came for the appreciation of its eruption. One day, when I was drawing diagrams on the balcony and he was bathing inside, the volcano erupted unexpectedly.

7
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:55,186
听：The ash and lava fountains shooting high in the sky varied from 50 to 100 meters in height. It was absolutely fantastic! I even noticed a rainbow appear in the fog caused by a heat wave.

8
00:01:55,186 --> 00:02:11,593
跟读：The ash and lava fountains shooting high in the sky varied from 50 to 100 meters in height. It was absolutely fantastic! I even noticed a rainbow appear in the fog caused by a heat wave.

9
00:02:11,593 --> 00:02:28,551
听：But, glancing through our surroundings, I foresaw the potential danger and found no guarantee of our safety. The uncomfortable gas almost made us unconscious. Sweat began to drip as we grew anxious.

10
00:02:28,551 --> 00:02:45,509
跟读：But, glancing through our surroundings, I foresaw the potential danger and found no guarantee of our safety. The uncomfortable gas almost made us unconscious. Sweat began to drip as we grew anxious.

11
00:02:45,509 --> 00:03:03,516
听：Managing to stop panicking and trembling, we quickly put on our protective suits, helmets and boots and eventually made our way to a safe place. How lucky we were even though my precious equipment and documents were all burnt to the ground!

12
00:03:03,516 --> 00:03:21,524
跟读：Managing to stop panicking and trembling, we quickly put on our protective suits, helmets and boots and eventually made our way to a safe place. How lucky we were even though my precious equipment and documents were all burnt to the ground!
